# Docker & DevOps Guidelines

Container orchestration defined in [docker-compose.yml](mdc:docker-compose.yml).

## Services

### Backend Service
- Image: Built from `./backend`
- Container: `journal-backend`
- Port: 5000
- Dependencies: db
- Environment: DATABASE_URL, OLLAMA_HOST
- Volumes: `./backend:/app`, `/app/node_modules`

### Frontend Service
- Image: Built from `./frontend`
- Container: `journal-frontend`
- Port: 3000
- Dependencies: backend
- Environment: REACT_APP_API_URL
- Volumes: `./frontend:/app`, `/app/node_modules`

### Database Service
- Image: `postgres:15-alpine`
- Container: `journal-db`
- Port: 5432
- Environment: POSTGRES_USER, POSTGRES_PASSWORD, POSTGRES_DB
- Volume: `./data/postgres:/var/lib/postgresql/data`

## Dockerfiles

### Backend Dockerfile [backend/Dockerfile](mdc:backend/Dockerfile)
```dockerfile
FROM node:18-alpine
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm install
COPY . .
EXPOSE 5000
CMD ["npm", "start"]
```

### Frontend Dockerfile [frontend/Dockerfile](mdc:frontend/Dockerfile)
```dockerfile
FROM node:18-alpine
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm install
COPY . .
EXPOSE 3000
CMD ["npm", "start"]
```

## Networking

- Backend connects to database via hostname: `db`
- Frontend connects to backend via `http://localhost:5000`
- Backend connects to Ollama via `host.docker.internal:11434`
- Extra hosts configured for Docker Desktop compatibility

## Volume Management

- Source code volumes for hot reloading
- Anonymous volumes for node_modules to prevent overwrites
- PostgreSQL data persisted in `./data/postgres`

## Best Practices

- Use `restart: unless-stopped` for all services
- Mount node_modules as volume to prevent container overwrites
- Use health checks (if needed)
- Keep environment variables in docker-compose.yml
- Never commit sensitive credentials to git
